WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.100
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Did you like school?

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.300
<v><b>Mark:</b></v> I loved school actually.

00:00:13.301 --> 00:00:17.460
Um, I think I preferred senior school more than junior school,

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.027
but yeah, um, lots of friends, lots of,

00:00:21.027 --> 00:00:23.700
sort of sporting activities and things, so yeah, I loved it.

00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:27.500
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What were your best and worst subjects?

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.035
<v><b>Mark:</b></v> My best subject was probably mathematics.

00:00:33.369 --> 00:00:41.420
Um, loved mathematics and found I was, sort of, very capable at it, so it was quite easy.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.497
Um, I think it’s one of those things that’s natural.

00:00:43.497 --> 00:00:47.380
But, um, worst subject, maybe Latin.

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:51.110
Never very good at languages even though I use them every day now,

00:00:51.113 --> 00:00:54.540
but never very, I like languages now, but I hated them at school.

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:08.180
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Did you have a favourite or least favourite teacher at school?

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.789
<v><b>Caroline:</b></v> Um, let me think about that.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:15.820
Yes, I, um, liked the French teacher.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:23.620
She was probably my favourite, favourite teacher because, um,

00:01:23.657 --> 00:01:30.180
she was French and she taught us to speak with a very good French accent.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.060
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Did she inspire you?

00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:36.820
<v><b>Caroline:</b></v> She did, and I’m still learning French and go,

00:01:36.843 --> 00:01:38.460
I live in Australia,

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:45.500
um, and I go to France every year and I go to French language schools.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.475
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have a problem making decisions?

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.704
What about?

00:01:56.853 --> 00:01:58.338
<v><b>John:</b></v> It depends what sort of decision it is.

00:01:58.363 --> 00:02:02.063
If it’s a sort of instant decision, I make pretty good instant decisions,

00:02:02.063 --> 00:02:05.740
but the longer you think about them, then I probably decide,

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:08.078
or try to decipher, which is the best decision.

00:02:08.078 --> 00:02:10.260
So, instant decision is a better way for me.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.460
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you know any twins?

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:21.580
Are they identical?

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.020
<v><b>Alison:</b></v> Yes, I’m a twin myself.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.460
I have a twin brother.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.420
And my sister has got twin boys.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.540
They’re aged 16 and they’re not identical.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:41.380
They don’t look very similar and they don’t have similar personalities either.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:50.540
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Who do you think gossips more, men or women? Why?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:56.024
<v><b>Kathy:</b></v> I think stereotypical-, stereotypically people say women gossip more,

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.718
um, but I actually think men gossip quite a lot as well.

00:03:01.718 --> 00:03:06.780
I think, I think men gossip more in a factual way, whereas women gossip more,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.060
maybe, in more of a personal, emotional way,

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.070
so maybe in kind of a nastier way than what men do, I would say.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:19.220
But I would say that they probably gossip the same, or in a similar way.